{"ref":"BDB, נֹ֫פֶת","hw":"נֹ֫פֶת","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">נֹ֫פֶת</span></big>  <strong>n.m.</strong> <sup><a data-ref=\"Proverbs 24:13\" href=\"/Proverbs.24.13\">Pr 24:13</a></sup> <strong>flowing honey, honey from the comb (</strong>Ph. <span dir=\"rtl\">נפת</span> CIS <sup>i. 166, 8 b</sup><strong>)</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">נ׳</span> abs. <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 5:3\" href=\"/Proverbs.5.3\">Pr 5:3</a> + 3 times, cstr. <a data-ref=\"Psalms 19:11\" href=\"/Psalms.19.11\">ψ 19:11</a>;—sweet <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 24:13\" href=\"/Proverbs.24.13\">Pr 24:13</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">דְּבַשׁ</span>), cf. <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 27:7\" href=\"/Proverbs.27.7\">27:7</a>; fig. of sweet words <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 5:3\" href=\"/Proverbs.5.3\">Pr 5:3</a>, and perhaps <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:11\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.11\">Ct 4:11</a> (Bu of kisses; ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">דְּבַשׁ</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">חָלָב</span>); in full <span dir=\"rtl\">נ׳ צוּפִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 19:11\" href=\"/Psalms.19.11\">ψ 19:11</a> <em>honey of</em> (<em>the</em>) <em>combs</em> (comp. with <span dir=\"rtl\">מִשְׁפְּטֵי י׳</span>; ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">דְּבַשׁ</span>).","next":"BDB, נֶפְתּוֹחַ","prev":"BDB, נֶ֫פֶת²"}